---
title: Verify an Alibi
description: Check a real Keelson Alibi in one command, with no account.
estimate: 1 minute, no account
section: Quickstart
order: 1
---

An Alibi is the public record of one purchase an AI agent made under a Keelson mandate. This guide checks a real one, from a purchase paid on the PayPal sandbox, against production.

{% walkthrough %}
{% steps %}
{% step title="Take a real Alibi" file="verify.sh" lines="1-2" %}
This Alibi was issued on 9 November 2026 and is committed to the repository as a test fixture, so it never changes under you.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Send it to the verifier" file="verify.sh" lines="4-8" %}
`POST /v1/alibis/verify` runs the browser verifier's checks against pinned trust roots and a public Arbitrum RPC. It needs no account, and it stores nothing.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Read the verdict" file="verify.sh" lines="9-11" %}
`verified 2of2` means both TEE legs, Intel TDX and AWS Nitro, countersigned this purchase, and every check that applies to it passed.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Do it from code" file="verify.ts" lines="5-12" %}
The same request from TypeScript. The idempotency key makes a retry the same request.
{% /step %}
{% step title="See what was checked" file="response.json" lines="4-12" %}
Each check names one thing it proves: the mandate's passkey, both attestations, the countersignature, inclusion in the public log, the witnesses and the anchor on chain. Checks for features this purchase did not use, such as zero-knowledge proofs, are `absent`.
{% /step %}
{% step title="Trust no server" file="verify.sh" lines="1-2" %}
Download [the same file](/samples/01M6ZWZJHWRRHQEYNJAT7NMSV8.alibi) and drop it on [verify.keelson.finance](https://verify.keelson.finance). The checks run in your browser against roots pinned in its code; only the chain reads leave your machine.
{% /step %}
{% /steps %}
{% files %}
```sh {% file="verify.sh" check="verify-one-command" %}
# A real Alibi from the PayPal sandbox, countersigned by both TEEs
ALIBI=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DavidZapataOh/keelson-paypal/main/packages/alibi/test/fixtures/01M6ZWZJHWRRHQEYNJAT7NMSV8.alibi

curl -sL "$ALIBI" \
| curl -s https://api.keelson.finance/v1/alibis/verify \
    -H 'content-type: application/vnd.keelson.alibi.v1+json' \
    -H "idempotency-key: docs-$RANDOM$RANDOM" \
    --data-binary @- \
| jq -r '"\(.verdict) \(.mode)"'

# expect: ^verified 2of2$
```
```ts {% file="verify.ts" %}
const alibi = await fetch(
  "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DavidZapataOh/keelson-paypal/main/packages/alibi/test/fixtures/01M6ZWZJHWRRHQEYNJAT7NMSV8.alibi",
).then((r) => r.arrayBuffer());

const res = await fetch("https://api.keelson.finance/v1/alibis/verify", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    "content-type": "application/vnd.keelson.alibi.v1+json",
    "idempotency-key": crypto.randomUUID(),
  },
  body: alibi,
});

const { verdict, mode, checks } = await res.json();
console.log(verdict, mode); // verified 2of2
```
